For \(x\in\mathbb{R}^n\) and \(\lambda>0\), define \(Q_{
obreak\lambda,x}(y)=f(y)+(2\lambda)^{-1}\|y-x\|^2\). The model is prox-unbounded at \((x,
obreak\lambda)\) when \(\inf_y Q_{
obreak\lambda,x}(y)=-
obreak\infty\). Equivalently, there exists a sequence \((y_k)\) such that \(Q_{
obreak\lambda,x}(y_k)	o-
obreak\infty\). In this regime the Moreau envelope value \(e_
obreak\lambda f(x)=
obreak\inf_y Q_{
obreak\lambda,x}(y)\) equals \(-
obreak\infty\), and the proximal solution set \(\operatorname*{argmin}_y Q_{
obreak\lambda,x}(y)\) is empty. The quadratic regularizer therefore does not dominate the negative growth of \(f\).

